ef 17592186045585] [17592186259046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258523 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259046 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259046 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259046 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186257819 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259046 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "047ad574-9503-5413-9fac-632c989f1e97" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186256913 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257185 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257636 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258388 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258671 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186258388 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259134 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "33b4cd81-c3a3-52e0-a0d4-355e8ea3aed5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257331 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257385 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257404 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257599 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257794 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186257331 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259403 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "ced03044-c848-5e8d-a236-e8367ae6dd32" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259134 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124192" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v+u+1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-3$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0a1ba57-9eac-5d49-9cdd-f7f25fec8c92" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259622 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v+u+1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259403 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124321" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v-u+2,\\,y=2u+v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-5$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6b75fa0-1178-5417-bc31-861bbdef5229" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259668 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v-u+2 \\\\ 2u+v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259046 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124561" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/79/79b09bcf02998adf6d7bf19e7d59cabdc563ff26266966440bbb49be53029ac3.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-\\frac{u+1}{2}\\le v\\le u+1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6fdc3f93-8486-56f6-8744-50fa49ca621b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186259696 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](images/53/539c74bf4d397916fd7ac11089fa9500bd71cdf2278891136785d6e792431b05.png)\n\n             \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-1,-1),(1,-1),$ and $(-2,2).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](images/ad/adfe476bd2ca719996d612855ca5368bdea09370b7befcffb08a062db8587cbb.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186408073 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186408074 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186408075 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1045 "The Image of an Affine Transformation" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186408074 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046665 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049041 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408072 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "eb78a48d-c31f-5955-bc9e-cdc4e0762d1c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408073 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408075 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408073 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a78ca60-8278-5f69-a0c5-4853a7109868" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408073 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259668 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408074 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408073 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408074 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "88a789c1-e3c2-5586-9aab-92005c1e4bcd" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408074 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259622 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408075 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de3c23cf-80a3-5af4-81aa-d8176ded4ab6" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186408075 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259696 #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
